  "body": "Don't know why but synctl isn't able to stop the daemon... Maybe a thread doesn't stop correctly ? I had to SIGKILL it...\r\n\r\n```\r\n(.synapse) root@matrix_container:~/.synapse# synctl stop\r\nstopped synapse.app.homeserver\r\n(.synapse) root@matrix_container:~/.synapse# synctl start\r\nsynapse.app.homeserver already running\r\n(.synapse) root@matrix_container:~/.synapse# tail -5 homeserver.log\r\n2017-12-30 17:04:40,332 - twisted - 131 - INFO - - Received SIGTERM, shutting down.\r\n2017-12-30 17:06:00,988 - twisted - 131 - INFO - - Received SIGTERM, shutting down.\r\n2017-12-30 17:06:02,298 - twisted - 131 - INFO - - Received SIGTERM, shutting down.\r\n2017-12-30 17:06:06,958 - twisted - 131 - INFO - - Received SIGTERM, shutting down.\r\n2017-12-30 17:19:09,283 - twisted - 131 - INFO - - Received SIGTERM, shutting down.\r\n(.synapse) root@matrix_container:~/.synapse# \r\n```",
